.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt DF 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm df
.Nd AMD Zen data fabric nexus driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /devices/df@*
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver represents each data fabric
.Pq DF
instance in the AMD Zen family processors used by the Oxide architecture.
Every I/O die implements a DF instance: the crossbar connecting its compute
complexes, memory controllers, and I/O subsystem to one another and, via
inter-socket links, to the fabrics of other sockets.
On all currently supported processors there is one I/O die, and therefore
one instance of
.Nm ,
per socket.
.Pp
Each device node's unit address is the fabric node ID of the DF instance it
represents, which is also available as the
.Sy node-id
property.
The nodes representing the I/O units attached to each die's fabric are
enumerated as children of the corresponding
.Nm
node.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioms 4D
